    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0865" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–3048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-30T12:00:00+08:00">November 30,
                            1948—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 30—3:10 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2364. Should Government move to Canton or elsewhere, I am convinced move will
                    represent effort Generalissimo to give space for time in desperate anticipation
                    increased American military aid. Should he move, it is likely that, motivated
                    almost solely by traditional Chinese official loyalty, those surrounding him who
                    owe him so much will accompany him.</p>
                <p>We believe our purposes would be facilitated if in this connection we could be
                    informed of the results of Mme. Chiang’s<anchor n="16" xml:id="d785-f1"/>
                    conversations in order that we may pass on, in our discretion, in undiluted form
                    to the ranking officials of the Government and possibly to the Generalissimo, US
                    official reaction to Madame’s pleas.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d785-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d785-f1" n="16" xml:id="d785-f1-content">
                <p>Wife of Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d785-f2" n="17" xml:id="d785-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 1812, December 13, 3 p. m., to the Ambassador in China, <ref
                        target="frus1948v08">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">viii</hi>
                    </ref>, “U.S. Military Assistance to China” (Ch. VII).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
